  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "What is Byculla known for?",
      "answer": "Byculla is known for the Byculla Zoo (Veermata Jijabai Bhosale Udyan) - Mumbai's oldest zoo - as well as its rich multi-community heritage spanning Jewish, Christian, Muslim and Hindu communities, the historic Byculla railway station, and being one of South Mumbai's most culturally layered and rapidly transforming localities."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the pin code of Byculla?",
      "answer": "Byculla has multiple pin codes: 400027 (Byculla East / Mazgaon) and 400008 (Byculla West / Nagpada / Clare Road)."
    },
    {
      "question": "What are the sub-areas within Byculla?",
      "answer": "The main micro-localities within Byculla are Mazgaon, Nagpada, Chinchpokli, Clare Road, Jacob Circle, Agripada, Dongri, Kamathipura, and the Byculla Zoo belt."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the property price in Byculla?",
      "answer": "Property prices in Byculla range from ₹70 lakh for a 1BHK in Nagpada/Chinchpokli to ₹1.5–2.5 Cr for a 2BHK in Mazgaon/Clare Road, and ₹2.5–4 Cr for premium new-development apartments near Jacob Circle. Rental rates range from ₹15,000 to ₹45,000 per month depending on the sub-area and flat size (as of May 2026)."
    },
    {
      "question": "How to commute from Byculla?",
      "answer": "Byculla is served by the Central Railway's Byculla Station (10 min to CST), Chinchpokli Station, BEST bus routes 1, 3, 63, 66, 83, 124, and direct access to the Eastern Freeway via Mazgaon. The area is also well-served by taxis and autos."
    },
    {
      "question": "Which hospitals are in Byculla?",
      "answer": "Major hospitals in and near Byculla include J.J. Hospital (Grant Medical College), Masina Hospital, Cama & Albless Hospital, St. George's Hospital, and Wockhardt Hospital."
    },
    {
      "question": "Which schools are in Byculla?",
      "answer": "Notable schools in Byculla include St. Mary's High School, Don Bosco High School, Holy Name High School, St. Anne's High School, and Anjuman-I-Islam School."
    },
    {
